work_phase.pseudocode:
AFTER production/tests pass:
  UPDATE F-34 header test paths only if the new focused test is now authoritative.
  UPDATE F-34 Section 1.2 evolution trace with the Phase 1 change and rationale;
    do not invent a commit/PR identifier before one exists.
  UPDATE F-34 Sections 2.1/2.2 scope and acceptance criteria with:
    - per-turn transcript source;
    - accepted root voice eligibility;
    - five exact continuous bands;
    - not-applicable null-points rule;
    - internal-only Phase 1 handoff;
    - overall score unchanged until Phase 4;
    - VAD/live accuracy not established.
  UPDATE F-34 Section 3 flow so transcript pair -> duration evaluator -> internal report metrics is explicit.
  UPDATE F-34 Section 4.1 with the actual new pure function signature/snippet and post-write line reference;
    quote only code that exists on disk after implementation.
  UPDATE F-34 Sections 5/6 with missing duration, stale aggregate, unknown mode, and debugging boundaries.
  UPDATE F-34 Section 7 with the per-turn-versus-aggregate ownership trade-off only if it remains accurate after implementation.
  APPEND one dated Phase 1 change-log entry with actual changed files and actual commands/results.
  MARK browser, live speech provider, human calibration, production, deployment as NOT RUN.

RUN focused tests, backend lint, diff checks, and forbidden-path checks.
THEN launch exactly one clean-context read-only auditor for Cycle 3.
AUDITOR reviews only task-owned diff + acceptance criteria + source contracts.
AUDITOR must return an evidence matrix for:
  exact band boundaries;
  N/A versus Level 1 distinction;
  turn exclusions and follow-up handling;
  text guard;
  canonical per-turn source;
  no overall-score mutation;
  no live-turn latency-path edits;
  docs truthfulness.
REPAIR only auditor-confirmed blocking gaps, rerun affected focused checks,
and ask the same auditor for the final matrix. Do not launch a second auditor.
